      "title": "INTRODUCTION",
      "kind": "intro",
      "page": 0,
      "text_preview": "M OST 10-Gb/s SONET transmitter and receiver designs are implemented as two separate chips [3]. Integration of the transmitter and the receiver on the same silicon substrate will result in lower power dissipation and also require less area on the system board, resulting in cost savings. However, there is a risk of degraded jitter performance due to crosstalk between the transmitter and receiver ph ..."
