      "title": "SONET TRANSCEIVER",
      "kind": "other",
      "page": 0,
      "text_preview": "A simplified application example of a SONET transceiver is shown in Fig. 1. The transceiver chip consists of the transmitter (TX) and receiver (RX). The optical data signal is fed into the receiver after being converted to an electrical signal by a transimpedance amplifier (TIA). The receiver extracts a 10-GHz clock from the nonreturn-to-zero (NRZ) data stream and deserializes this into 16 paralle ..."
